    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.07), who represent our strongest offensive engines. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a quintessential plus-matchup against Brandon Pfaadt; the combination of a favorable park factor and a high stolen base probability\u2014aided by Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery\u2014positions him as our primary catalyst for both R and SB production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an elite cornerstone in the #2 hole, facing a favorable matchup against Cristian Javier (5.27 xERA). While Javier\u2019s skill set typically commands respect, his current volatility provides an ideal environment for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** to drive high-RBI output despite the neutral park metrics.\n\nOur middle-tier starters offer significant upside via platoon advantages and park factors. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.57) is a particularly strong play today, as his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed McGreevy drives his score well above his base projection. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** (57.84) secures a spot in the OF5 slot due to a massive +14% park factor, which helps mitigate a challenging matchup against the southpaw Ian Seymour. **Andy Pages** (61.68) and **Kyle Tucker** (65.22) also benefit from playing against Matthew Boyd; despite the potential for defensive suppression, the volume of high-leverage at-bats for both **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** keeps them firmly in the strong start tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was the inclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (52.94) over potential bench depth. While **Nasim Nunez** faces an elite arm in Aaron Nola, his sheer necessity as a stolen base anchor in our 5x5 build provides unique value that raw scoring efficiency sometimes misses. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined due to team off-days, and **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL, our roster flexibility is at its nadir. We must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for all starters, particularly **Heliot Ramos**, as any unfavorable shift in batting order could further compress these marginal scores and force a re-evaluation of our efficiency-based thresholds before first pitch.",
